WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.200
- [Baz] Standing by.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Crew] Marker.
(marker claps)

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.470
- And action.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.220
- Oscar memories.
(Rian vocalizing)

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.540
- Can it just be any memory?

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.373
- Yeah.
(inspirational music)

00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:11.310
- Well, my biggest memory is

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.830
when Julia Roberts won for Erin Brockovich

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.222
and I just remember the way
she sauntered up on the stage.

00:00:16.222 --> 00:00:17.580
(audience cheering)
(Julia laughing)

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.080
- I remember Olivia Coleman's speech

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.400
which I thought was a class speech.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.870
(audience cheering)
- Thank you.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.703
- Billy Crystal.

00:00:22.703 --> 00:00:23.610
And Billy Crystal.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:24.720
And Billy Crystal.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.580
- The thing that was most powerful for me

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.473
was being able to meet people whose words

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:32.902
and works inspired me.

00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:35.665
(Santiago speaking Spanish)

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:36.652
(Ricardo laughing)

00:00:36.652 --> 00:00:40.860
(Santiago continues speaking Spanish)

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.190
- You had Spielberg, you had
Jack Nicholson down the front.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.590
- Next to him, there was Warren Beatty.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.600
- It scared the crap outta me.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.520
- I thought I'd be able to be a cool cat

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.090
who stays chill, but I
emphatically was not.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.520
- Instead of saying cheers with my drink,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.500
I said cheers with the Oscar.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.962
And accidentally I got a
big scratch on my Oscar.

00:01:01.962 --> 00:01:03.210
(Anders laughs)

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.740
And I'm not sure to this day

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.770
if Brad Pitt also has a
scratch on his Oscar. (laughs)

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.740
- Actually met Snoop Dogg,
got a selfie with him.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.460
It's still the picture on my
Facebook page to this day.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.320
- I remember my father-
- [Baz] Oh God.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.550
- Who was my date,

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.550
running away from me at the speed of light

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.440
because he'd seen Julie Andrews

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.090
and was determined to have a
long conversation with her.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.400
- The shoe of my wife fell very low

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.710
into the dungeons of the theater,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.561
so you know why she had just one shoe.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.714
(audience cheering)

00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:36.720
- I think about Oscars,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.790
mostly it's just about
a celebration of art.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.850
- I absolutely loved the moment when Rayka

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.250
won for "Period. End of sentence" in 2019.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.170
- Period. End of sentence.
(crowd cheering)

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.420
- I always looked at Leo's career

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.683
and getting to see him go
up there for "The Revenant",

00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.440
I felt very happy for him.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.740
- That was the Oscars that Darlene Love,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.560
one of the greatest voices
in American music history

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.731
brought the house down.

00:01:59.731 --> 00:02:01.710
♪ And I know ♪

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.200
- I remember when "Parasite" won.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.759
- Parasite.
(audience cheering)

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:07.750
- The entire room just exploded

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.170
and I have no idea what it
felt like watching it on TV,

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.390
but in the room, it felt
like a rock concert.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.620
- The "Parasite" sweep

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.230
was one of the greatest
things that's ever happened.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.250
- We had one of those nights

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.190
where we had 11 wins
out of 11 nominations.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.060
- Lord of the Rings.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.020
- Lord of the Rings.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.060
- Lord of the Rings,
the Return Of the King.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.000
- And we partied in Peter
Jackson's room all night long.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.370
- Myself and my whole family,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.700
we were in front of the
TV with all excitement

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.249
when my friend Mr. AR Rahman-

00:02:35.249 --> 00:02:36.360
- AR Rahman.
(crowd cheers)

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.750
- Surprisingly he got two
Oscars on the same day.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.510
- We had a projector
and a projection screen

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.740
and cooked up a storm.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.240
And we're watching the awards.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.240
And Joel and Ethan win for
best original screenplay.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.000
- Ethan and Joel Cohen, for "Fargo".

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:52.833
(crowd cheers)

00:02:52.833 --> 00:02:54.000
- And in the middle of
the speech, Joel says-

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.520
- I'd like to thank everyone
over at Mary Zophres' house.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.810
I guess this woke you guys up.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.260
- And the room, my house went bonkers.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.420
It was one of the most special experiences

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.833
and evenings of my life.

